  "id": "Compound::DB00588 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Fluticasone Propionate is implicated in the regulation of Cyp3a4 through a series of binding interactions involving serine proteases and glucocorticoids. The evidence suggests that Fluticasone Propionate binds to Serpina6, which is then bound by either Ciclesonide or Prednisolone, both of which ultimately interact with Cyp3a4. This indicates a potential pathway where Fluticasone Propionate may influence Cyp3a4 through the action of these glucocorticoids. The lowest common ancestors of these interactions point to the broader category of therapeutic glucocorticoids, suggesting a shared biological role in modulating enzyme activity. The scores from the paths are consistent, indicating a plausible but not definitive relationship. The mechanism involves the binding of Fluticasone Propionate to a serine protease, which then mediates the interaction with Cyp3a4, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
